    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d666-a7">

                <pb facs="0994" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg866"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No. 22.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Robeson to the
                            governor-general of Syria</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 1,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Highness</hi>: I hasten to inform your highness that
                    I have received information that the Mutassarif of Acca, in obedience to
                    instructions received, has ordered the kaimahan of Safed to expel the American
                    citizens residing there, who I understand to be Louis Lubrowsky <pb facs="0995"
                        n="867" xml:id="pg867"/> and brother. These gentlemen are citizens of the
                    United States and are entitled to the protection of the American Government, and
                    I declare their expulsion without due process of law, conviction of crime, or
                    misdemeanor to be illegal and in violation of international courtesy and treaty
                    stipulations existing between the United States and the Sublime Porte.</p>
                <p>I protest against any American citizen being illegally molested or interfered
                    with by the Turkish authorities.</p>
                <p>I request your highness to arrest all proceedings against the gentlemen referred
                    to, and please let me know at your earliest convenience what course your
                    highness has deemed proper to take in this important matter.</p>
                <p>I improve, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN T. ROBESON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
